! STEOM-DLPNO-CCSD def2-SVPD AutoAux RIJCOSX TightSCF TightPNO
# ITEM 1 of the revision compute list: GAS-PHASE control for Table 1
# (Reviewer 2, minor point 3). Identical geometry, method, basis and %mdci block
# to the SUCCESSFUL embedded run weekend_dipole/steom_def2_svpd.inp
# (532.8 nm), with %pointcharges removed. Nothing else differs, so the
# embedded-minus-gas shift is method-matched.
#
# Geometry md5 6d55e271fea4a37f19c9a803406e5c48 -- byte-identical to the
# embedded run and to dipole_gauge/.
#
# Why the three earlier attempts failed (neo_model/orca_steom/, 12-13 Aug):
#   gas_control       MPI rank abort (signal 6) in MDCI
#   gas_control_retry stalled in the PNO stage
#   gas_robust        "Not enough memory for ABMV!" at %maxcore 4000 x 8
# All three are memory/MPI, NOT active-space failures. The embedded run cleared
# the same basis and geometry at 5000 x 8, so this asks for 6000 x 8 = 48 GB of
# the 53 GB free.
#
# OThresh/VThresh are deliberately LEFT AT DEFAULT 1e-3. The 2026-06-30
# diagnosis in neo_model/orca_steom/gas_robust/steom_gas.inp records that the
# ORCA 6.1 manual warns against lowering them -- a larger active space pulls in
# MORE doubles-polluted states. DoDbFilter + NRootsCISNAT are the reproducibility
# fix, and both are already on and already matched to the embedded run.
%maxcore 5000
%pal nprocs 8 end
%mdci
  NRoots 5
  DoRootWise true
  FollowCIS true
  RootHoming true
  CheckEachRoot true
  DTol 1e-5
  DoStoreSTEOM true
  AddL2Term True
  DoDbFilter true
  NRootsCISNAT 10
  TCutPNOSingles 1e-12
  NDav 400
  MaxIter 400
end
* xyzfile -1 1 geom_cthrp.xyz
